# LLM profile: local (AB#67/AB#70). No key, no quota, nothing leaves the
# machine — see docs/04-development/setup.md's "Local LLM (Ollama)" section.
#
# Non-secret provider/model/timeout defaults only. `scripts/dev.sh up local`
# loads this file first, then `.env` on top of it — `.env` holds only
# secrets (GEMINI_API_KEY, JWT_SECRET, ...) and machine-specific overrides,
# never a provider choice, so switching profiles never means hunting through
# `.env` for a stale LLM_PROVIDER line. Don't edit `.env` to switch modes;
# run `scripts/dev.sh up cloud` instead.
#
# `OLLAMA_BASE_URL`'s port (11435) is this project's own — deliberately not
# Ollama's default 11434, which on a machine running another project's
# Ollama container (or a bare `ollama serve`) is already taken. `dev.sh`
# starts and owns a native `ollama serve` on this port; it never touches
# whatever else is listening on 11434.
LLM_PROVIDER=split
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11435/v1
OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen3:8b
OLLAMA_VISION_MODEL=qwen2.5vl:3b
OLLAMA_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=600
OLLAMA_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120
LLM_ENABLE_FALLBACK=false
